<LegalPage title="Trust & Security — GetMine.ai" description="How GetMine.ai approaches trust and security — honest about today, deliberate about what we’re building toward." canonical="https://getmine.ai/trust.html">
    <p class="page-eyebrow">Trust &amp; Security</p>
    <h1 class="page-headline">Your vault stays with you.</h1>

    <p class="page-lead">GetMine is built so your health information can work for you without giving up control. This is how we approach trust and security today, and what we&rsquo;re building toward.</p>

    <div class="page-section">
      <h2>Local-first by design</h2>
      <p>Your vault lives on your device. The day-to-day work of organising and recalling your information happens locally, on hardware you own.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="page-section">
      <h2>Minimum necessary exposure</h2>
      <p>We aim to send only the smallest slice of context needed for each task, and only when you ask. Your full health record never has to leave your vault.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="page-section">
      <h2>You decide what leaves</h2>
      <p>Sharing happens by choice. You decide what is shared, with whom, and for how long. You can revoke access at any time.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="page-section">
      <h2>Transparency matters</h2>
      <p>We want you to be able to see how GetMine works, what it does with your information, and what is changing. We&rsquo;ll continue to publish plain-English documentation as the product matures.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="page-section">
      <h2>A foundation, not a destination</h2>
      <p>Security is foundational and we treat it that way. As GetMine matures, our security posture will continue to deepen &mdash; more controls, more transparency, and progressively more of the architecture running at the edge.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="page-section">
      <h2>Honest about today</h2>
      <p>We&rsquo;re a small team in closed beta. We have not yet sought formal certifications (such as SOC 2 or ISO 27001) and we don&rsquo;t make claims we can&rsquo;t back up. We will pursue the right ones as the product and the team grow. Until then, what we promise is what we build: a local-first vault, minimum necessary exposure, and your data under your control.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="page-section">
      <h2>Questions</h2>
      <p>Write to <a href="mailto:privacy@getmine.ai">privacy@getmine.ai</a> for any trust or security question. We&rsquo;ll answer honestly.</p>
    </div>
</LegalPage>
